# Build artifacts
/target/
*.log
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Per-crate build output
!Cargo.lock

# Python bytecode (scripts/, docs/eval/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Luxe-specific
.luxe/
# Verification captures — throwaway evidence for one session, megabytes of it.
.pi/agent-loop/screenshots/
.pi/agent-loop/shots/
# The coding agent's own notes, including summaries it writes when it compacts a conversation.
# Whatever was on screen ends up in here verbatim, so a key pasted into a chat becomes a tracked
# file, and the next `git add -A` commits it. Untracked on purpose; keep durable prose in docs/.
.pi/memory/
/*.png

# Website build artifacts. `web/src/assets/generated` is deliberately NOT ignored: it is derived
# from this repo, and CI checks it is current.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
# Wrangler's dev-server scratch: caches, a shim worker, and its source maps.
web/.wrangler/

# The phone app's type checker, test libraries and browser driver
crates/luxe-remote/app-tests/node_modules/
web/.astro/

# cargo-mutants scratch output
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# Driver notes from a recording take. Useful while a demo script is being written and worthless
# afterwards; the cast beside them is the artifact.
web/src/assets/captures/*.log
web/src/assets/captures/*.raw.cast
# What a take said and sent, kept for auditing one that went somewhere unexpected; see site-record.sh
web/src/assets/captures/*.wire.jsonl
web/src/assets/captures/*.session.jsonl
